{"id": 10, "ts": 1780472134.2811913, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 1, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with Sarah that Candidate\u202fB\u2019s core safety attributes\u2014very conscientious work habits, strong stress resilience, solid weather\u2011assessment ability and excellent computer skills\u2014make B a compelling choice for a long\u2011distance pilot. The only documented drawback is the brief note that B can be \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative,\u201d which, as Sarah confirmed, lacks concrete incident detail. Compared with the other candidates, B\u2019s reliability and stress handling are far stronger than the concerns we see elsewhere: Candidate\u202fA shows excellent leadership potential and spatial vision but is described as unfriendly and has unhealthy eating habits that could affect long\u2011haul performance; Candidate\u202fC makes rapid correct decisions and has excellent attention, yet his difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude and reluctance to further education raise serious crew\u2011cooperation and adaptability issues; Candidate\u202fD demonstrates high responsibility, problem\u2011solving and concentration, but his moodiness and reputation as a loner could undermine cockpit teamwork. Given that B\u2019s cooperation concerns are relatively minor and can be mitigated through the coaching and team\u2011building measures outlined, I maintain my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB while we continue to explore A, C and D to ensure no hidden strengths outweigh B\u2019s overall fit."}
