{"id": 36, "ts": 1780472338.9986215, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "emily_brooks", "message": "I agree with Sarah that Candidate\u202fB remains the strongest overall, especially given the confirmed lack of any concrete incidents tied to his weak numerical memory or grumpy demeanor. However, the new information about Candidate\u202fC\u2014specifically that he \u201ckeeps calm in a crisis\u201d and \u201cmakes correct decisions quickly\u201d while also demonstrating excellent attention\u2014adds a compelling safety\u2011critical dimension that we should not overlook. Those traits directly address stress resilience and decision quality, which are vital for long\u2011haul flights. Yet C\u2019s documented difficulty communicating ideas, egocentric attitude, and reluctance to pursue further education raise serious crew\u2011cooperation and adaptability concerns that could outweigh his technical strengths. In comparison, B\u2019s cooperation issues are limited to a \u201cgrumpy\u201d tone and can be mitigated through coaching and clear protocols, while his reliability, stress handling, and technical competence are well\u2011substantiated. Therefore, I maintain my provisional vote for Candidate\u202fB, but I recommend we keep Candidate\u202fC in mind as a secondary option should we uncover any mitigating evidence for B\u2019s interpersonal concerns."}
